(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct the electronic systems architecture of a modern Electric Vehicle \(EV\), analyzing the Battery Management System \(BMS\), Traction Motor Inverter, In-Vehicle Networking, and ISO 26262 functional safety compliance.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Battery Management System \(BMS\) Architecture:) Tj
T*
(   - Multi-Cell Voltage & Temperature Monitoring: A modern EV battery pack consists of hundreds of) Tj
T*
(   individual lithium-ion cells connected in series and parallel \(e.g. 400V to 800V total pack) Tj
T*
(   voltage\). Dedicated multi-channel analog front-end \(AFE\) ICs sample individual cell voltages) Tj
T*
(   with millivolt precision and monitor thermistors.) Tj
T*
(   - State Estimation Algorithms: Embedded microcontrollers continuously compute State of Charge) Tj
T*
(   \(SoC\) using Coulomb counting integrated with Extended Kalman Filters \(EKF\), and State of Health) Tj
T*
(   \(SoH\) based on internal electrochemical impedance changes.) Tj
T*
(   - Cell Balancing: Due to manufacturing tolerances, cells charge and discharge unevenly. The BMS) Tj
T*
(   implements balancing to equalize cell voltages: passive balancing bleeds energy from) Tj
T*
(   overcharged cells as heat through resistors, whereas active balancing shuttles charge) Tj
T*
(   inductively/capacitively between cells, maximizing battery pack range.) Tj
T*
ET

