T*
(   2. Technical Architecture & Hardware Abstraction Layers \(HAL\):) Tj
T*
(   - Bare-Metal Firmware: Interacts directly with hardware registers using memory-mapped I/O) Tj
T*
(   pointers. Critical concepts include configuring system phase-locked loops \(PLLs\), interrupt) Tj
T*
(   vector tables, direct memory access \(DMA\) controllers, and bit masking.) Tj
T*
(   - Hardware Abstraction Layer \(HAL\): Provides standardized software APIs that decouple) Tj
T*
(   application code from target silicon registers, allowing firmware to be ported across different) Tj
T*
(   microcontroller families \(e.g., STM32 to NXP\) with minimal rewriting.) Tj
T*
(   - Low-Level Bus Drivers: Implementing robust communication drivers for UART, SPI, I2C, and CAN) Tj
T*
(   buses incorporating hardware FIFO buffers, DMA circular buffers, and non-blocking state machine) Tj
T*
(   interrupts.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Real-Time Operating System \(RTOS\) Thread Management:) Tj
T*
(   - Task Scheduling: Modern embedded systems employ RTOS kernels \(e.g. FreeRTOS, Zephyr\)) Tj
T*
(   featuring preemptive priority-based schedulers. Tasks are assigned deterministic priorities and) Tj
T*
(   execute within isolated stack spaces.) Tj
T*
(   - Inter-Task Communication & Synchronization: Utilizing thread-safe FreeRTOS Queues,) Tj
T*
(   Binary/Counting Semaphores, Mutexes with Priority Inheritance to prevent priority inversion,) Tj
T*
(   and Event Groups.) Tj
T*
(   - Power Management & Tickless Idle: Configuring low-power sleep modes where the CPU enters deep) Tj
T*
(   sleep during idle periods and wakes up only upon external hardware interrupts, extending) Tj
T*
(   battery operation to years.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Industrial Career Opportunities & Employers:) Tj
T*
(   - High global demand across automotive electronics \(Bosch, Continental, Tesla\), consumer) Tj
T*
(   electronics \(Apple, Dyson, Sony\), industrial automation \(Siemens, Schneider Electric\), and) Tj
T*
(   medical devices \(Medtronic, Philips\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
