(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering \(GATE\) for Electronics and Communication Engineering \(EC\), detailing its examination structure, syllabus weightage, PSU recruitment avenues, and postgraduate career impact.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Structure and Purpose of GATE \(EC Paper\):) Tj
T*
(   - The Graduate Aptitude Test in Engineering \(GATE\) is an all-India standardized examination) Tj
T*
(   administered jointly by the Indian Institute of Science \(IISc\) and seven Indian Institutes of) Tj
T*
(   Technology \(IITs\) on behalf of the Ministry of Education.) Tj
T*
(   - Exam Structure: 3-hour computer-based test comprising 65 questions totaling 100 marks.) Tj
T*
(   Sections include General Aptitude \(15 marks\), Engineering Mathematics \(13 marks\), and Core ECE) Tj
T*
(   Technical Subjects \(72 marks\). Questions consist of Multiple Choice Questions \(MCQ\), Multiple) Tj
T*
(   Select Questions \(MSQ\), and Numerical Answer Type \(NAT\) questions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Syllabus Decomposition and Topic Weightage:) Tj
T*
(   - Engineering Mathematics: Linear algebra, calculus, differential equations, complex variables,) Tj
T*
(   probability and random variables, numerical methods.) Tj
T*
(   - Networks, Signals and Systems: KCL, KVL, network theorems, transient analysis,) Tj
T*
(   continuous/discrete-time Fourier series and transforms, Laplace and Z-transforms, LTI systems.) Tj
T*
(   - Electronic Devices & Analog Circuits: Energy bands in silicon, p-n junctions, Zener diodes,) Tj
T*
(   BJTs, MOSFETs, diode circuits, BJT/MOSFET amplifiers, frequency response, feedback amplifiers,) Tj
T*
(   op-amps, active filters, and oscillators.) Tj
T*
(   - Digital Circuits: Number systems, Boolean algebra, combinational logic, sequential circuits) Tj
T*
(   \(flip-flops, counters, shift registers\), memory, 8085 microprocessor.) Tj
T*
(   - Communications: Random processes, noise, analog modulation \(AM, FM\), digital modulation \(ASK,) Tj
T*
(   PSK, QAM\), information theory, Shannon capacity, error control coding.) Tj
T*
(   - Electromagnetics: Maxwell's equations, uniform plane waves, transmission lines, Smith chart,) Tj
T*
(   waveguides, dipole and horn antennas.) Tj
T*
