(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct the architecture of an AUTOSAR-compliant Electronic Control Unit \(ECU\) in automotive systems, explaining the MCAL, Basic Software \(BSW\), Runtime Environment \(RTE\), and Application Layer.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Need for AUTOSAR \(AUTomotive Open System ARchitecture\):) Tj
T*
(   - Modern luxury automobiles contain between 80 to 150 independent Electronic Control Units) Tj
T*
(   \(ECUs\) interconnected by multiple networks. Prior to AUTOSAR, automotive software was tightly) Tj
T*
(   coupled to specific microcontroller hardware, making software reusability virtually impossible) Tj
T*
(   and supplier changes prohibitively expensive.) Tj
T*
(   - AUTOSAR establishes an open, standardized software architecture that completely decouples) Tj
T*
(   automotive application software from the underlying microcontroller silicon.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Four Hierarchical Software Layers:) Tj
T*
(   - Microcontroller Abstraction Layer \(MCAL\): The lowest software layer consisting of device) Tj
T*
(   drivers that directly access microcontroller hardware registers \(e.g., ADC, PWM, CAN, SPI,) Tj
T*
(   Flash drivers\). MCAL provides standard APIs to upper layers, so changing microcontrollers) Tj
T*
(   requires updating only the MCAL.) Tj
T*
(   - Basic Software \(BSW\): Provides essential background services divided into functional stacks:) Tj
T*
(   \(1\) Communication Stack \(CAN, LIN, Ethernet communication services\); \(2\) Memory Stack \(NVRAM) Tj
T*
(   manager, Flash EEPROM emulation\); \(3\) System Stack \(OS scheduling, watchdog manager, ECU state) Tj
T*
(   management\); \(4\) Diagnostic Stack \(UDS ISO 14229 diagnostics\).) Tj
T*
(   - Runtime Environment \(RTE\): The central nervous system of AUTOSAR. It acts as a virtual) Tj
T*
(   communication bus that interconnects Application Software Components \(SWCs\) with each other and) Tj
T*
(   with the BSW. Whether two software components communicate across internal CPU registers or) Tj
T*
(   across an external physical CAN bus, the software component code remains 100% identical?the RTE) Tj
T*
(   handles communication transparently via Virtual Functional Bus \(VFB\) mapping.) Tj
T*
(   - Application Layer: Contains the core automotive control algorithms \(e.g., Anti-lock Braking) Tj
T*
(   System - ABS, Adaptive Cruise Control, Engine Torque Management\) encapsulated in modular) Tj
T*
(   Software Components \(SWCs\) authored in C or auto-generated from MATLAB Simulink models.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 14:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the role and architecture of Hardware Security Modules \(HSM\) and Hardware Root of Trust \(RoT\) in embedded IoT and automotive electronic systems, detailing cryptographic engines and secure boot lifecycles.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Cybersecurity Threat to Hardware Electronics:) Tj
T*
(   - As microcontrollers connect to public internet clouds \(IoT\) and vehicles become) Tj
T*
(   software-defined connected terminals, electronic systems face severe cyber threats?including) Tj
T*
(   unauthorized firmware flashing, remote vehicle hijacking, intellectual property theft, and) Tj
T*
(   differential power analysis side-channel attacks. Software-only security is fundamentally) Tj
T*
(   insufficient if the underlying hardware is compromised.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

