(   [Problem Statement]: Analyze the emergence of Wide-Bandgap \(WBG\) semiconductors: Gallium Nitride \(GaN\) and Silicon Carbide \(SiC\), comparing their material properties against silicon, and detailing applications in EV power electronics and 5G RF.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Physical Material Property Comparison:) Tj
T*
(   - Silicon has dominated the electronics industry for 60 years. However, its fundamental) Tj
T*
(   physical properties?bandgap energy Eg = 1.12 eV, critical breakdown electric field Ec =~ 0.3) Tj
T*
(   MV/cm, and thermal conductivity k =~ 1.5 W/\(cm*K\)?impose severe operating limits in high-power,) Tj
T*
(   high-voltage, and high-frequency environments.) Tj
T*
(   - Silicon Carbide \(4H-SiC\): Wide bandgap Eg = 3.26 eV \(3x silicon\), breakdown field Ec = 3.0) Tj
T*
(   MV/cm \(10x silicon\), thermal conductivity k = 4.9 W/\(cm*K\) \(3x silicon\). SiC can withstand much) Tj
T*
(   higher breakdown voltages \(up to 1200V-1700V\) in vastly thinner drift layers with 100x lower) Tj
T*
(   on-state resistance \(Rds_on\).) Tj
T*
(   - Gallium Nitride \(GaN\): Wide bandgap Eg = 3.4 eV, breakdown field Ec = 3.3 MV/cm, and) Tj
T*
(   exceptionally high two-dimensional electron gas \(2DEG\) electron mobility \(mu = 2000 cm^2/\(V*s\)\)) Tj
T*
(   in AlGaN/GaN High Electron Mobility Transistors \(HEMTs\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. High-Efficiency Electric Vehicle Applications \(SiC Power MOSFETs\):) Tj
T*
(   - EV Traction Inverters: SiC MOSFETs replace bulky silicon IGBTs. Because SiC has near-zero) Tj
T*
(   reverse recovery charge and ultra-fast switching speeds, switching energy losses drop by up to) Tj
T*
(   75%.) Tj
T*
(   - System-Level Benefits: 98.5%+ inverter efficiency extends EV battery driving range by 5% to) Tj
T*
(   10% on an identical battery pack. Higher thermal conductivity allows much smaller, lighter) Tj
T*
(   cooling heatsinks, reducing overall vehicle mass.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. 5G RF Base Station Power Amplifiers \(GaN HEMTs\):) Tj
T*
(   - High Frequency & Power Density: GaN RF transistors deliver 5 to 10 times higher RF power) Tj
T*
(   density per square millimeter than silicon LDMOS at microwave and millimeter-wave frequencies) Tj
T*
(   \(3.5 GHz to 40 GHz\).) Tj
T*
(   - Massive MIMO Front-Ends: Enables ultra-compact, lightweight 64T64R massive MIMO active) Tj
T*
(   antenna units mounted directly on cellular towers with exceptional Power-Added Efficiency) Tj
T*
