(   [Problem Statement]: Deconstruct the architecture and career landscape of Deep-Tech Hardware Entrepreneurship in India, detailing the India Semiconductor Mission \(ISM\), Design Linked Incentive \(DLI\), and Fabless startup incubation.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Deep-Tech Hardware Revolution in India:) Tj
T*
(   - For decades, India's technological reputation was dominated by IT software services. However,) Tj
T*
(   a major paradigm shift is underway toward deep-tech hardware engineering?spurred by soaring) Tj
T*
(   domestic electronics consumption, geopolitical supply chain realignment, and visionary national) Tj
T*
(   semiconductor policies.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The India Semiconductor Mission \(ISM\) & Policy Framework:) Tj
T*
(   - The Government of India established the India Semiconductor Mission \(ISM\) with a historic) Tj
T*
(   budgetary outlay of $10 Billion \(INR 76,000 Crores\) to build a robust semiconductor and display) Tj
T*
(   manufacturing ecosystem.) Tj
T*
(   - Financial Support Pillars: \(1\) 50% fiscal support on a pari-passu basis for setting up) Tj
T*
(   Silicon Semiconductor Fabs and Display Fabs; \(2\) 50% fiscal support for setting up Compound) Tj
T*
(   Semiconductor / Silicon Photonics / OSAT assembly and packaging facilities; \(3\) Chips to) Tj
T*
(   Startup \(C2S\) program training 85,000 specialized VLSI engineers across 100+ academic) Tj
T*
(   institutions.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Design Linked Incentive \(DLI\) Scheme & Fabless Startups:) Tj
T*
(   - The DLI scheme specifically targets domestic fabless chip design startups, offering up to 50%) Tj
T*
(   reimbursement of eligible expenditure \(up to INR 15 Crores per company\) for product) Tj
T*
(   development, EDA tool license access, and foundry tape-out costs.) Tj
T*
