(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the technical domain and career responsibilities of an Electronic Product Quality, Reliability, and Failure Analysis \(FA\) Engineer, detailing accelerated life testing, bathtub curve, and decapping microscopy.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. The Imperative of Semiconductor Reliability:) Tj
T*
(   - Designing an integrated circuit that operates in a laboratory is insufficient; the chip must) Tj
T*
(   function continuously for 10 to 15 years inside an automotive engine compartment, an undersea) Tj
T*
(   telecom cable, or a satellite in space without hardware failure. Reliability and Failure) Tj
T*
(   Analysis \(FA\) engineers ensure silicon components survive operational stress throughout their) Tj
T*
(   intended lifecycle.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. The Bathtub Curve and Accelerated Stress Testing:) Tj
T*
(   - The Bathtub Curve: Models component failure rate over time, characterized by: \(1\) Infant) Tj
T*
(   Mortality Period \(early failures due to latent manufacturing defects\); \(2\) Useful Life Period) Tj
T*
(   \(low, constant failure rate driven by random events\); \(3\) Wear-Out Period \(sharply increasing) Tj
T*
(   failure rate due to physical degradation like electromigration and gate oxide breakdown\).) Tj
T*
(   - Burn-In Testing: Subjecting chips to elevated operating voltages \(1.2x Vdd\) and high) Tj
T*
ET

